WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
outriders is a game that isn't defined  by big new ideas  but a variety of familiar elements mixed  together in experimental ways  it's a role-playing game with loot  shooter elements it's a serious dark  sci-fi story with a big dose of  goofiness and humor  it's a cover shooter that demands you  rush out and smash enemies with  ludicrous superpowers  whether this mixture works for you will  determine how much you'll enjoy it  [Music]  though outriders looks like a loot  shooter live game  it's actually much more mass effect 3  than destiny 2.  like in mass effect rpg progression and  cover shooting are much more important  than chasing the next new gun  outriders is a cover shooter rpg with a  hearty dose of gear progression  leaning heavily into an epic story told  with tons of dialogue cut scenes and  collectible lore  developer people can fly draws a lot  from its past work on the gears of war  series  rifle-toting enemies take fortified  positions to unload on you at a distance  backed up by shotgunners that try to  close the gap armored troops with chain  guns plotting in the open  and cleaver wielding sprinters who  charge straight at your face to drive  you out of cover  the core of outriders is shooting and  you'll have a mess of guns at your  disposal  though you can only have two main  weapons and a sidearm equipped at any  given time  you'll have lots of options thanks to  loot shooter half of the outrider's  formula  that means you can pair a sniper rifle  with a shotgun or assault rifles with  smgs and since you're constantly  searching for weapons with better stats  you'll cycle through a lot of different  loadouts in a short amount of time  what makes these guns especially fun are  the myriad different properties and  status effects they can have  like dispensing poison blowing enemies  up freezing people solid  and so on recalling gears of war again  outrider shooting reliably feels good  but finding synergies between your  weapon's weird properties  is a lot of what makes the shooting part  of the game rewarding  things get a bit weirder as outriders  merges space superpowers with its cover  shooter core  you could choose from one of four  character classes early in the game  devastator trickster pyromancer or  technomancer  these each have the general roles of  tank rogue  damage focused mage and debuff focus  mage the devastator uses gravity attacks  for close range kills  the trickster teleports around to get  the drop on enemies  the pyromancer is a mid-range  fireflinger and the technomancer can  summon turrets and rockets  that also poison or slow targets each  class has a different way of  replenishing health through combat  generally by focusing on their specific  strengths the devastator for instance  heals you for every close range kill  encouraging you to get in close to  enemies to hit them with powers like a  small earthquake  combat becomes a constant calculus  between when to cut the distance and  take down an enemy  and when to take cover bide your time  and protect yourself  that combination can be a bit confusing  and as a result  combat is a place where outriders can  both sprint and stumble  you're playing a shooter where you use  cover to keep yourself alive  but you're encouraged to leave cover to  keep yourself alive  that push and pull of avoiding incoming  damage and taking the fight to the enemy  means that you constantly have to be  managing the battlefield  as well as your ability cooldown timers  if you jump out of cover and go wild  with all your powers on an approaching  enemy  you leave yourself exposed for all their  friends and quickly find yourself cut  down by incoming fire  that means that having an earthquake  ready to stun incoming fighters  is essential to saving your life since  it allows you to grab kills  while keeping your head down similarly  abilities like the trickster's teleport  which instantly puts you behind enemies  who are in cover are just as useful for  dramatically repositioning yourself  across the battlefield  as they are for eliminating foes but you  can rarely just go all out with your  guns and abilities you really have to  think about where you are  where your enemies are and how you can  best eliminate them without exposing  yourself  it can feel unintuitive for a while but  when you do find the balance between  using your powers  healing yourself and staying out of fire  outriders can create some pitched  frantic battles that use cover just  enough to give you a second to breathe  without nailing your shoulder to a  single chest high wall  and leaving you there for minutes on end  but there are also times when you'll  find yourself surrounded or cut off  trapped between enemies unable to kill  anything fast enough  or escape the onslaught to save yourself  sometimes a situation will just feel  unwinnable  but luckily outriders generally sets you  back only a bit when you die  so you can re-enter a fight quickly and  try a new approach  facing tougher altered enemies who have  power similar to yours  can result in battles of attrition where  you have to cheese the situation  by scurrying out of the arena so enemies  don't all chase you down at once  sometimes even careful management of  powers cover  and your spacing on the battlefield  aren't enough to save you  and it's these moments when outriders  can get frustrating because it doesn't  feel like you're losing for lack of  skill there are ways to deal with that  issue  outriders is largely pretty open and has  liberal fast travel  so you can bail on a mission and go do  side quests to grab rewards that can  boost your gear and character  the difficulty of enemies is also  determined by your overall world  tier level which rises as you earn  experience points  alongside your character level world  tier also determines loot drops  so there is an incentive to keep it on  the highest level you can  but if you're in a particularly annoying  fight you could always back it down a  touch to keep yourself from stalling  the world tier is a smart solution to  the difficulty problem  and since it can be adjusted anytime it  gives you a lot of freedom to avoid  frustration at key moments  while the combat can be tough to wrap  your head around at first the frenetic  balancing act has created some heart  pounding moments  more fun and intense battles than  annoying ones you can also play out  riders in co-op which really elevates  how frantic and wild combat can become  having multiple super powered players  working together makes for a bombastic  sensory overloading combat experience  outriders is best experienced with  friends and other players  co-op continually highlights the game's  best features  and encourages you to think creatively  about combining powers  guns battlefield control and teamwork  unfortunately playing together has been  tough since out writer's launch  cross play between consoles and pc is  currently disabled  and some players have complained of  server connection issues while i didn't  encounter any connection problems while  i played solo on pc  i did have repeated crashes when  connecting with friends  and trying to play together on console  the server issues are even worse  with lengthy wait times when loading  into the game and unexpected disconnects  when playing  those technical issues will likely get  cleaned up over time  but right now it's frustrating that the  game's always online nature  means even those playing in single  player are stuck dealing with some of  the problems  people can fly has said it's working to  improve the experience  but so far the most frustrating thing  about the game has been those times when  i crashed to desktop  when trying to play with friends when it  comes to its narrative  i enjoyed outrider's lengthy story  although it winds up being more  disjointed than what was implied in the  first half or so  people can fly has obviously put a lot  of time and thought into the game's lore  and there's a lot of interesting writing  to be found in the journal entries and  side quests  enoch the planet where outriders takes  place was meant to be an idyllic new  world for the remnants of humanity to  colonize  instead it's a war-torn hellscape where  the last vestiges of the human race are  ripping each other apart  the misery and torment of the situation  is exacerbated by the altered  like your character who have gained  godlike powers  unfortunately the longer it goes on the  less outriders mixes  its intense topics and blockbuster-like  humor  things get dark as time goes on but the  road trip style story  abandons examining how to handle being a  human-turned god  and instead looks into atrocities  related to scientific ethics  and colonialism in the end it feels like  outriders shift subjects a few times  leaving a lot of the threads hanging and  without bringing many to a satisfying  conclusion  but the moments where outriders is  taking daring swings  at mixing disparate elements are when  it's at its best  the game is surprisingly deft at  combining things that  shouldn't work together to make  something new and fun especially when  you've got friends with you  and put the time in to really understand  the game's systems  outriders rewards you with epic battle  moments and a sprawling scope  it left me wanting to continue venturing  out into the wilds of enoch  to see what i might find there and to  smash whatever it was  with seismic earthquake magic  [Music]  you

